    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "defined-translator"
      },
      "source": [
        "# **Data Preperation**\n",
        "\n",
        "Once we have loaded the dataset, we preprocess the data as follows:\n",
        "\n",
        "Add a start and end token to each sentence.\n",
        "\n",
        "Clean the sentences by removing special characters.\n",
        "\n",
        "Create a word index and reverse word index (dictionaries mapping from word → id and id → word).\n",
        "\n",
        "Pad each sentence to a maximum length."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 10,
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2024-09-12T04:18:26.642341Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2024-09-12T04:18:26.641993Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2024-09-12T04:18:26.646444Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2024-09-12T04:18:26.645469Z",
          "shell.execute_reply.started": "2024-09-12T04:18:26.642307Z"
        },
        "id": "secret-spouse",
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Restrict the total number of sentences to 70000\n",
        "NUM_SENTENCES = 70000"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 11,
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2024-09-12T04:18:26.648083Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2024-09-12T04:18:26.647698Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2024-09-12T04:18:28.643260Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2024-09-12T04:18:28.642327Z",
          "shell.execute_reply.started": "2024-09-12T04:18:26.648053Z"
        },
        "id": "hearing-synthetic",
        "outputId": "c384c192-132d-428f-b695-1193b7de47c3",
        "trusted": true,
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Input sentence type: <class 'str'>\n",
            "Output sentence type: <class 'list'>\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# strip the input and output of extra unnecessary characters\n",
        "# store all the cleaned input and output sentences into input_sentences[] and output_sentences[]\n",
        "# tokenize the Hindi (target) sentences using the indicNLP libary class and add <sos> (start-of-sentence) and <eos> (end-of-sentence)\n",
        "\n",
        "from indicnlp.tokenize import indic_tokenize\n",
        "\n",
        "input_sentences = []\n",
        "output_sentences = []\n",
        "\n",
        "# Read English sentences (source language)\n",
        "with open('train.en', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
        "    for count, line in enumerate(f, 1):\n",
        "        if count > NUM_SENTENCES:\n",
        "            break\n",
        "        input_sentence = line.rstrip().strip(\"\\n\").strip('-')\n",
        "        input_sentences.append(input_sentence)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Read Hindi sentences (target language)\n",
        "with open('train.hi', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
        "    for count, line in enumerate(f, 1):\n",
        "        if count > NUM_SENTENCES:\n",
        "            break\n",
        "        output_sentence = line.rstrip().strip(\"\\n\").strip('-')\n",
        "        # Tokenize Hindi sentences using indicNLP library\n",
        "        tokens = indic_tokenize.trivial_tokenize(output_sentence)\n",
        "        # Append start and end tags to the tokenized sentences\n",
        "        output_sentences.append(['<sos>'] + tokens + ['<eos>'])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Input sentence type: {type(input_sentences[10])}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Output sentence type: {type(output_sentences[10])}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 12,
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2024-09-12T04:18:28.644687Z",
